Ranged Sneak Attack	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialAttack.Sneak Attack.Peerless Archer Class Feature	DEFINE:RangedSneakAttackDieSize|0	DEFINE:RangedSneakAttackDice|0									DESC:+%1d%2|RangedSneakAttackDice|RangedSneakAttackDieSize																												BONUS:VAR|RangedSneakAttackDieSize|6|TYPE=Base																																				ASPECT:NAME|Ranged Sneak Attack +%1d%2|RangedSneakAttackDice|RangedSneakAttackDieSize

Ranged Sneak Attack				KEY:Peerless Archer ~ Ranged Sneak Attack				CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class Feature.Peerless Archer Class Feature.SpecialQuality.SneakAttack.Sneak Attack																																						DEFINE:PeerlessArcherSneakAttackLVL|0	DEFINE:RangedSneakAttackDice|0	DESC:You can do an additional %1d6 damage if your opponent is unable to defend against you - whenever your opponent would be denied any dex bonus to AC, or you are flanking. At range (up to 30'). Creatures immune to critical hits are also immune to this sneak bonus.|SneakAttackDice	DESC:If a rogue can catch an opponent when he is unable to defend himself effectively from her attack, she can strike a vital spot for extra damage. Basically, the peerless archer's attack deals extra damage any time her target would be denied a Dexterity bonus to AC (whether the target actually has a Dexterity bonus or not), or when the rogue flanks her target. This extra damage is 1d6 at 1st level, and it increases by 1d6 every three peerless archer levels thereafter. Should the peerless archer score a critical hit with a sneak attack, this extra damage is not multiplied. (See Table 8-5: Attack Roll Modifiers and Table 8-6: Armor Class Modifiers, page 151, for combat situations in which the peerless archer flanks an opponent or the opponent loses his Dexterity bonus to AC.) Ranged attacks can count as sneak attacks only if the target is within 30 feet. You can't strike with deadly accuracy from beyond that range.  You can sneak attack only living creatures with discernible anatomies-undead, constructs, oozes, plants, and incorporeal creatures lack vital areas to attack. Any creature that is immune to critical hits is not vulnerable to sneak attacks. You must be able to see the target well enough to pick out a vital spot and must be able to reach such a spot. You cannot sneak attack while striking a creature with concealment (see page 152) or striking the limbs of a creature whose vitals are beyond reach.|PREVAREQ:DisplayFullAbility,1																																	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Ranged Sneak Attack																BONUS:VAR|RangedSneakAttackDice|(PeerlessArcherSneakAttackLVL+2)/3	BONUS:VAR|PeerlessArcherSneakAttackLVL|PeerlessArcherLVL				SOURCEPAGE:p.115

